{
    "_about": [
        "How each distinction badge looks. A badge = a template (families) + layers applied in order.",
        "A layer lists element ids of the template and the attributes to set on them:",
        "  fill / stroke = a colour (#rrggbb) or a gradient of the template (url(#chrome), url(#silver), url(#navy))",
        "  display = none (hide) or inline (show)",
        "  transform = move or resize a part, e.g. translate(-5,-10) or scale(1.1)",
        "  text = what is written in a text element",
        "  viewBox, width, height (id badge) = the size of the picture, for badges that grow (archers, cards)",
        "  data-figure = which drawing of figures.svg goes in a slot (the animal of a set)",
        "The pictogram parts (logo.svg) are ink (the archer), bow and cam (compound only).",
        "Embroidered badges (round, frame, archers, marmot): felt = the cloth, thread-1 to thread-4 = the four",
        "  tones of the thread (the same colour four times for a plain thread, light and dark tones for gold",
        "  and silver), ring / frame stroke-width = twice the thickness of the ring or frame seen.",
        "Drawings: figures.svg holds the drawings in use, each under its id. Another version of a drawing can be",
        "  added there under an id of its own (squirrel-b...); to use it, change the name in the layer of the",
        "  animal (\"squirrel\": {\"figure\": {\"data-figure\": \"squirrel-b\"}}), or for the archers in the base of",
        "  the family archers (\"archer-shape\": {\"data-figure\": \"archer-b\"}).",
        "The archers badge is the frame badge (badge-frame.svg) with its archers shown: the family archers sets",
        "  its sizes, so the frame keeps the thickness of the 3D badges.",
        "Thresholds, and which layers make which badge: rules.json.",
        "tiles: the levels not drawn yet show as a text tile, bg = background, fg = text; its border",
        "  comes from tile_borders (the column's tile in rules.json, default otherwise).",
        "chart: colour of a level's line on the archer's chart; without it, the plate colour of its",
        "  layer, else the tile colour."
    ],
